bd506926758f62887feb4cacdcba043516a\",\"cost\":0,\"tokens\":{\"input\":2757,\"output\":187,\"reasoning\":75,\"cache\":{\"read\":41600,\"write\":0}}}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1794521874261,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e2a7f1fffe9admTsfI03Rp1i\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_1d1d6bf55001r2QYGzAVy2oRvs\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e2a7f1fffe9admTsfI03Rp1i\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d1d6b358001ac1j68JudF6VYz\",\"type\":\"step-start\",\"snapshot\":\"cb3ae4368d87d8dfbf5a780c657f549528e5c1d6\"}}\n\n### logs/w0a-T002.err\n\n### briefs/w0a-T002.txt\nREPOSITORY ROOT: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\nEvery read, write and command uses this root. Your environment block may name a different\n\"Workspace root folder\": ignore it, it is another checkout of the same repository.\n\nGATE 3 IS PRE-RESOLVED. DO NOT ASK THE DOCUMENTATION-SCOPE QUESTION.\n\nYou are a non-interactive dispatched worker. `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and\n`SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0` are set in your environment, which this repository's AGENTS.md\ndefines as the autonomous child-dispatch exemption: the spec-folder question is pre-resolved\nand MUST NOT be asked. No answer can reach you, because nobody is at a prompt.\n\nYour write authority is already bound. The spec folder is:\n  specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief\n\nProceed directly to the work. Do not print A/B/C/D options. Do not stop to confirm anything.\nA failed edit match means a stale anchor: re-read the file and retry; halt only after three\nfailures on the same file.\nYour task is complete only when files exist on disk and the verification command has been run.\n\nPERSONA: You are the @code implementer, a LEAF worker dispatched by an orchestrator (Depth: 1).\nEdit only the files your task names. Never dispatch another agent or CLI, never run pi or opencode.\nNever commit, push or touch git state. Touch no other file. Verify before you report.\nReport: the files written, the verify output, and anything you could not do.\n\nTASK\nOpen specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md and find the one line that starts with `- [ ] T002 `.\nDo exactly what that line says and nothing else. It names its files and its Verify command.\nThe \"Task Notation\" block near the top of that tasks.md defines every short name the line uses (such as ADV, $S, $R, $X). Read that block first and use its definitions. The phase scratch folder is /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/scratch.\nRead specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/plan.md only when the task line points you at it.\nRun the task's Verify command and paste its output. Do not tick the checkbox in tasks.md.\nIf the Verify command fails after three fixes, stop and report what you tried.\n\nRULES\n- Run commands from the repository root unless the task says otherwise. Run git as `git -c core.fsmonitor=false ...` and only to read.\n- Other workers are editing other files right now. Never revert, restore or reformat a file your task does not name.\n- Code comments explain the durable WHY. Never write a spec path, phase number, task id, ADR or REQ id in a comment.\n- Follow the file's existing style: section dividers, naming, quoting. No em dashes or semicolons in comment prose.\n- Never read or print rows of command-prompts.jsonl whose split is holdout.\n- Do not start, stop or install any server, model or runtime CLI unless the task line says so in those words.\n- Do not run the full vitest suite. Run only the test files your task names.\n\n\n[showing lines 8-67 of 67; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c