{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794521896860,"sessionID":"ses_e2e2a7f1fffe9admTsfI03Rp1i","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1d7150f001xbO8AGC4gm35Qc","sessionID":"ses_e2e2a7f1fffe9admTsfI03Rp1i","messageID":"msg_1d1d702900016EmecEjeYWk7Pk","type":"tool","id":"call_b9bdc432c13f432ab696bfd0","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"Advisor: ","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor","limit":60},"output":"Found 60 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:\n  Line 44: The single front door is the daemon-backed CLI at `.skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs`, which speaks the advisor's own newline-delimited protocol over a unix socket. When the daemon is unreachable, the CLI answers from the Python scorer at `runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py` and marks the response degraded, so the prompt-time brief reports `Advisor: stale` rather than claiming live. The skill also owns the documentation for the OpenCode plugin surface and the `/goal` plugin.\n\n  Line 105: - When there is no brief, the plugin and the hooks emit a fallback that opens with one status line (`Advisor: outage (...)`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.`).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ROUTER.md:\n  Line 333:   - If the daemon stays unreachable, the CLI answers from the local Python scorer and marks the result degraded. The brief then renders `Advisor: stale` instead of claiming live.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:\n  Line 39: 5. **Render.** `renderAdvisorBrief` produces the model-visible `Advisor:` text. When there is no brief, the handler emits `renderAdvisorFallbackDirective`: one status line, then the directives block. The line reads `Advisor: outage (<status>)` with the command to route by hand when the advisor failed or timed out, `Advisor: no skill matched.` when it answered with nothing above threshold, and `Advisor: prompt skipped.` when the prompt gate declined. The `/doctor:setup` hint appears on no-match and outage lines for prompts that use set up, set-up or setup wording, install or reinstall wording including installation and installer, configure or configuration wording or `check` followed within three words by environment, env, config, hooks, tools, tooling, toolchain or skilled. The no-match line ends with ` For setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup.` The outage line places `for setup or health checks, run /doctor:setup;` before the hand-route command so it stays last. Raw prompt text is never persisted in diagnostics, cache metadata, status, or attribution.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:\n  Line 2: title: \"Skill Advisor: Manual Testing Playbook\"\n\n  Line 7: # Skill Advisor: Manual Testing Playbook\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/directive-lifecycle-vectors.json:\n  Line 3:   \"brief\": \"Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.91/0.23 pass.\\nDirectives:\\n- Comment hygiene\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md:\n  Line 82: | SAD-003 | Claude hook additional context | Confirm prompt-time hook surfaces advisor context and fails open safely | `Role: Runtime hook operator. Context: current MCP server build and Claude UserPromptSubmit hook script. Action: pipe a realistic prompt payload into the hook, capture stdout and stderr separately and inspect additional context plus diagnostics. Format: return PASS or FAIL with context presence, prompt-safety result and exit code.` | 1. `bash: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime run build` -> 2. `bash: mkdir -p /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook` -> 3. `bash:` resolve `DIAG` with `advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())` and record its line count, as in step 2 above -> 4. `bash: printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"help me commit my changes\",\"cwd\":\"'\"$PWD\"'\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\"}' \\| SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1 node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js > /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.stdout.json 2> /tmp/skill-advisor-playbook/cl-001.shim-stderr.txt` -> 5. `bash: echo \"Exit: $?\"` -> 6. `bash: tail -n 1 \"$DIAG\"` -> 7. `bash:` pipe the same payload into `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` and capture its stderr | Exit code 0. Stdout is valid JSON and contains `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. For a matching prompt it starts with `Advisor:` and a freshness word (`live` or `stale`). With no brief it starts with one of the three status lines: `Advisor: outage (`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` `{}` means the shim failed, which is a FAIL. The shim's own stderr is empty. The diagnostics JSONL gains one line, and that record has `runtime: \"claude\"`, `emittedBytes` and `directivesSuppressed`. The inner hook's stderr carries the same record shape. The raw prompt literal is absent from both | Preconditions:<br>`SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=UNSET`<br>`hook script exists`<br><br>Shim transcript, 2026-09-26, stdout ab...\n  Line 87: - Stdout contains `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`. For a matching prompt it starts with `Advisor:` and a freshness word (`live` or `stale`). With no brief it starts with one of the three status lines: `Advisor: outage (`, `Advisor: no skill matched.` or `Advisor: prompt skipped.` `{}` means the shim failed, which is a FAIL.\n\n  Line